Yesterday I ascended for the second time, and for the first time as a
fighter.  The game was pretty smooth overall . . . notables:


- Orcus didn't have a /oD.  Just magic missile.  Bummer.

- When I got to the temple at Moloch's Sanctum, there was no high
priest.  There was a pile of priestly goods, but no corpse, and no
Amulet of Yendor.  By and by, Yeenoghu and Rodney showed up together .
. . I dispatched Rodney with a /oD and fought my way back to the
stairs to fight Yeenoghu, and HE had the Amulet.  Apparently, of his
own accord, he had killed the High Priest and stolen the Amulet before
I even got there.

- I had my choice between Cleaver, Vorpal Blade, and Demonbane.  I
tried #twoweaponing Vorpal and Demonbane for a while, but the +6
Cleaver ultimately won my affection.

- I learned a ton of spells, but never used any of them to good
effect.  After getting skilled in Attack spells, the best fail rate I
ever saw on anything was 78% (that's with Gauntlet of Power off, Helm
of Brilliance on, and all other armor "spell safe").  Is this
next-to-uselessness really the best a Barbarian can do?

- I had to buy all my protection a total of three times due to two
stupid mistakes: 1) neutral humans shouldn't sacrifice humans (doh!)
and 2) werewolves count as humans too (doh!).  After buying protection
twice, there wasn't enough gold in the game to buy it all again
(including the loot from Ludios) . . . hmmm, where can I get lots of
gold?  Let's just say the third donation was to a different priest.

- The "mysterious force" didn't bother me at all until I got to
Juiblex's swamp, which I had to cross six times in a row.  This was
the one level I was hoping NOT to keep crossing, because Rodney had
already stolen the Heart of Ahriman once and I was convinced he was
going to show up and do it again, drowning me.

- Like my first ascension, I died once choking over food.  Thank you,
"oLS.  There's a pattern here . . . at least this time it was somewhat
defensible (wraith corpse), unlike the first ascension (fortune
cookie).

- I saved up four potions of gain level until I reached the Astral
Plane, where I chugged them all in a row.  The already-generated
monsters suddenly seemed much wimpier.


